>Is there any way to connect to the tournament server that will not
>result in having to play in a monochromatic (all green) CRT window?
>Oh, and I also don't know how to get my number_pad turned on either...

To get colour:

1) Download Simon Tatham's thoroughly excellent telnet/SSH client, PuTTY,
   as advised by the devnull website.

      http://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/putty/

   You'll need to configure PuTTY to announce its terminal type as
   "xterm-color", because the combination of OpenBSD and Nethack is
   fascistic about colour support (OpenBSD in "standards fascism"
   shocker :-)

   It should be noted that Microsoft's own telnet client is (or at
   least, has always been in my experience) so broken it's painful to
   use.

2) Use the 'O'ptions command in Nethack to set the "color" option to
   "on".

Couldn't tell you whether you need to do anything special to your PuTTY
get number_pad support, though. (It's a loooooong time since I've tried
to use number_pad mode to play Nethack.)
